            <div xml:id="d775">

                <pb facs="0731" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">698.002/1007: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Butrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-03-24T15:00:00+08:00">March 24, 1940—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 28—1:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>245. Chungking’s 134, March 19, 10 a.m., and previous. Inspector General in
                    letter dated yesterday informed me that he has been authorized by telegram from
                    Minister of Finance at Chungking to act at his discretion in regard to
                    resumption of customs activities at Nanking and Chinkiang when the Yangtze is
                    reopened to foreign trade.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping and Chungking. Code text by air mail to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Butrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
